  "notes": "The employees-by-country table in the Annual Report 2024 (Sustainability Report, 'Employees and non-employees') covers 71 countries and territories and sums to its stated total of 614,082. It excludes the Chinese joint ventures; including them, the Group had 679,472 employees. The Group management report also gives a percentage split by market including the joint ventures (Germany 43%, Europe excl. Germany/Other 30%, Asia-Pacific 15%, North America 7%, South America 5%), which is not recorded because it is on a different basis. China's row is printed without a thousands separator ('23555'). The report says the production network has 115 production sites, 70 of them vehicle plants, but the plant map is a graphic with no machine-readable list, so plants are not counted by country. Sites are named in the report text; the Wolfsburg headquarters address (Berliner Ring 2) is quoted from the report's voting-rights notices. The report has no U.S. state breakdown, and no taxes-by-country table: a search for 'country-by-country', 'taxes paid' and 'tax contribution' found only Group and divisional income taxes paid. A separate Volkswagen tax transparency report was not checked.",
